{"findings":[{"tipo":"GC","causa_raiz":"Alocação massiva de memória na Heap a cada frame dentro do método Update, causada por concatenações de strings em loop (s += i.ToString()), alocação desnecessária de arrays grandes (new object[10000]) e chamadas repetidas a GameObject.FindObjectsOfType<GameObject>(), que além de alocar novos arrays gera custo de busca O(N). Esse excesso de lixo dispara coletas frequentes do Garbage Collector (GC.Collect atingindo ~17.94ms), bloqueando a thread principal e estourando o orçamento de 16.7ms.","codigo_refatorado":"using System;\\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\\nusing System.Text;\\nusing UnityEngine;\\n\\nnamespace PerformanceAdvisor.StressTest\\n{\\n    public class StressTestScene : MonoBehaviour\\n    {\\n        public bool stressGc = false;\\n        public bool stressCpu = false;\\n        public bool stressDraw = false;\\n        public GameObject testPrefab;\\n\\n        [Range(1, 20)]\\n        public float spawnRadius = 10f;\\n\\n        [Range(1, 50)]\\n        public int cubesPerFrame = 1;\\n\\n        public bool useUniqueMaterials = false;\\n\\n        [Range(1, 512)]\\n        public int cpuScansPerFrame = 1;\\n\\n        public int emptyObjects = 0;\\n        public int gcConcatIterations = 1000;\\n        public int gcArrayAllocs = 0;\\n        public int overdrawLayers = 0;\\n        public Material overdrawMaterial;\\n\\n        [Range(0, 2000)]\\n        public int prepopulateCount = 0;\\n\\n        private readonly StringBuilder _stringBuilder = new StringBuilder(4096);\\n        private readonly List<GameObject> _trackedObjects = new List<GameObject>();\\n        private MaterialPropertyBlock _propBlock;\\n        private static readonly int ColorPropId = Shader.PropertyToID(\\\"_Color\\\");\\n\\n        private void Awake()\\n        {\\n            _propBlock = new MaterialPropertyBlock();\\n        }\\n\\n        private void Start()\\n        {\\n            if (prepopulateCount > 0 && testPrefab != null)\\n            {\\n                for (int i = 0; i < prepopulateCount; i++)\\n                {\\n                    SpawnOne();\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            for (int i = 0; i < emptyObjects; i++)\\n            {\\n                var go = new GameObject(\\\"Empty_\\\" + i);\\n                _trackedObjects.Add(go);\\n            }\\n\\n            if (overdrawLayers > 0 && overdrawMaterial != null)\\n            {\\n                BuildOverdrawLayers();\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        private void BuildOverdrawLayers()\\n        {\\n            Camera cam = Camera.main;\\n            if (cam == null) return;\\n            float halfFov = cam.fieldOfView * 0.5f * Mathf.Deg2Rad;\\n            for (int i = 0; i < overdrawLayers; i++)\\n            {\\n                float d = cam.nearClipPlane + 0.05f + i * 0.001f;\\n                float h = 2f * d * Mathf.Tan(halfFov) * 1.1f;\\n                var quad = GameObject.CreatePrimitive(PrimitiveType.Quad);\\n                Destroy(quad.GetComponent<Collider>());\\n                quad.name = \\\"Overdraw_\\\" + i;\\n                quad.transform.SetParent(cam.transform, false);\\n                quad.transform.localPosition = new Vector3(0f, 0f, d);\\n                quad.transform.localScale = new Vector3(h * cam.aspect, h, 1f);\\n                quad.GetComponent<Renderer>().sharedMaterial = overdrawMaterial;\\n                _trackedObjects.Add(quad);\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        private void Update()\\n        {\\n            if (stressGc)\\n            {\\n                _stringBuilder.Clear();\\n                for (int i = 0; i < gcConcatIterations; i++)\\n                {\\n                    _stringBuilder.Append(i);\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            if (stressCpu)\\n            {\\n                for (int k = 0; k < cpuScansPerFrame; k++)\\n                {\\n                    int count = _trackedObjects.Count;\\n                    for (int j = 0; j < count; j++)\\n                    {\\n                        var obj = _trackedObjects[j];\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            if (stressDraw && testPrefab != null)\\n            {\\n                int n = Mathf.Max(1, cubesPerFrame);\\n                for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n                {\\n                    SpawnOne();\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        private void SpawnOne()\\n        {\\n            var clone = Instantiate(\\n                testPrefab,\\n                UnityEngine.Random.insideUnitSphere * spawnRadius,\\n                Quaternion.identity);\\n\\n            _trackedObjects.Add(clone);\\n\\n            if (useUniqueMaterials)\\n            {\\n                var renderer = clone.GetComponent<Renderer>();\\n                if (renderer != null)\\n                {\\n                    renderer.GetPropertyBlock(_propBlock);\\n                    _propBlock.SetColor(ColorPropId, new Color(\\n                        UnityEngine.Random.value,\\n                        UnityEngine.Random.value,\\n                        UnityEngine.Random.value));\\n                    renderer.SetPropertyBlock(_propBlock);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"Em C#, strings normais não podem ser modificadas depois de criadas. Quando usamos 's += ...' dentro do Update, o jogo cria milhares de novos textos na memória RAM gerenciada por segundo. Quando a lixeira (Garbage Collector) enche, ela precisa congelar o jogo por vários milissegundos para limpar essa bagunça, o que gera as famosas travadinhas (stuttering). Além disso, usar GameObject.FindObjectsOfType vasculha toda a cena a cada frame e cria uma lista nova toda vez. Na solução corrigida: (1) usamos StringBuilder reutilizável em vez de concatenar texto puro; (2) guardamos os objetos criados em uma lista própria (cache) em vez de varrer a cena inteira; (3) usamos MaterialPropertyBlock para alterar cores sem duplicar materiais na memória de vídeo nem quebrar o batching de renderização.\"}],\"dicas_level_design\":null}``` Eliminating the outer markdown block as requested:{"   
  ,"explicacao_didatica"
